<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Mobistar loses 4.19 bln Bfr in first year.</title>
<headline>Belgian Mobistar loses 4.19 bln Bfr in first year.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in billions of Belgian francs)</p>
<p>    Cons net loss	   4.190  vs  n/a</p>
<p>    Cons sales/turnover   0.699  vs  n/a</p>
<p>    Operating costs	 4.427  vs  n/a</p>
<p>    Current loss	    4.022  vs  n/a</p>
<p>    Financial loss	  0.294  vs  n/a</p>
<p>    Exceptional charges   0.168  vs  n/a</p>
<p>    Investments	    17.603  vs  n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - Belgian mobile phone company Mobistar launched Belgium's second GSM mobile phone network in August 1996.</p>
<p>In a statement released at a news conference on 1996 results, Mobistar said the loss was in line with expectations, taking into account start-up costs.</p>
<p>Mobistar said it now had more than 120,000 customers, up from 68,000 at the end of 1996, which was three times as many as forecast.</p>
<p>Mobistar said that after a capital increase last week, it was 57 percent owned by France Telecom. Belgian data communications company Telinfo holds 10 percent and nine other Belgian companies the balance.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
